WEBVTT

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:06.260
Chapter 3:

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:06.260
Birth of the 7th Platoon

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:10.900
Corporal Matt Connery.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.090
Yes, Ma'am.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.750
You're assigned to Squad 3.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:14.850
Yes, Ma'am.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.360
Sergeant Emal Wize.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:17.200
Yes, Ma'am.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.530
You're also in Squad 3.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:19.790
Yes, Ma'am.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.620
Superior Private Young Brum.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.400
Yes, Ma'am.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.140
You're assigned to Squad 6.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.750
2nd Lieutenant Welkin Gunther.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.380
Yes, Ma'am.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:28.840
Gunther?

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.760
You mean that Gunther?

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.760
You're appointed as the commanding officer of Squad 7.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.640
What's wrong? You have any objections?

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:39.100
No, Ma'am.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.420
It's a given.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.540
You were trained in armour in high school.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.780
At university, you completed an officer cadet course.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:53.030
Moreover, you are the son of General Gunther, otherwise known as the Hero of Gallia.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:58.350
But Captain Varrot, I have no actual combat experience.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.360
If you suddenly appoint me as the squad leader...

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.260
I have heard of your heroics at the Battle of Bruhl.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:07.560
I already consider you to have real combat experience.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.810
If that's the case, I have one request.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.130
What is it? Speak.

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:17.090
May I have permission to use the battle vehicle that I've brought from Bruhl?

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.260
Battle vehicle?

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:24.430
That vehicle has its quirks, so very few people are capable of maintaining it.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:25.800
So...

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.060
<i>I see, so that's how it is.</i>

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:37.560
Very well. Corporal Isara Gunther will be assigned to Squad 7.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:38.570
Thank you, Ma'am.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:46.220
Lieutenant Gunther. From now on, you will become the center of attention in more ways than one.

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:47.560
I await your victories.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.380
Sergeant Alicia Melchiott.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.250
Yes, Ma'am!

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:57.160
You will be aiding Lieutenant Gunther as Squad 7's non-commissioned officer.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:00.300
Mind your words!  Your confirmation?

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:04.160
Y-Yes, Ma'am! I'll be aiding Lieutenant Gunther!

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.050
Superior Private Susie Evans.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:06.860
Yes, Ma'am!

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:13.230
<i>Why on earth do I have to become Welkin's subordinate out of all people?!</i>

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:17.190
How did that happen? Why did I...

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:19.500
What's wrong?

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.080
Nothing's wrong...

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:26.500
You'll never understand how I feel!

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:34.310
I proudly volunteered for the Militia, but yet, I have to pair up with this weirdo?!

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.780
Lieutenant Welkin Gunther!

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:40.220
Yo. It's been a long time, Welkin.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:44.470
Faldio! You're Faldio!

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:50.640
Have some.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:53.590
Thank you.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:54.870
Is that so?

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:57.190
So you also joined the Militia?

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:00.820
Yes, I'm the commander of Squad 1.

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.900
So you didn't join the Military.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:06.310
Well, not really.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:09.830
So how are you two related?

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:11.680
We're in the same year in university.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:15.720
Welkin was taking biology, and I was majoring in archeology.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:19.930
You two are close, even though you're in different majors.

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:23.260
How do I explain it...

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.890
If you ask me...

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.500
It's a case of eccentric people being attracted to each other.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.190
Right! That may be so!

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:35.150
<i>Which means this person is also an oddball?</i>

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.530
But I'm surprised, Welkin.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:42.950
I never expected you to join the Militia so quickly.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:47.840
Since you really hate fighting that much, why?

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:52.920
I'm no exception to the policy of universal conscription, am I?

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.720
You're lying.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:04:00.300
There exist countless ways to avoid conscription, and you should be able to escape abroad.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:06.260
When Bruhl was occupied, I was also there.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.310
When I saw people dying before my eyes...

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:16.650
When I saw the town destroyed and the mill broken, I thought to myself,

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:22.110
'I must end this war as soon as possible.'

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:27.370
In order to return to that place once more, I have to fight as well.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:28.950
Welkin.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.030
I see.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.920
Welcome to the Militia.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:39.300
We are comrades-in-arms from this moment onwards.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.670
Yeah.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.010
Squad, stand in line!

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:50.680
Now the newly appointed commander of Squad 7 will give a welcome speech.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:52.840
Well then, Wel-

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:56.790
Lieutenant Gunther.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:58.700
It's fine, you don't have to force yourself.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:04.450
I'm Welkin Gunther, and I will be fighting together with you from today onwards.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.060
Nice to meet you.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:14.150
Everyone, let's not bother with the stiff formalities, shall we?

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:14.940
A-At ease!

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:23.270
Damn greenhorn from university.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:28.560
He's got zero combat experience and he's already putting on airs.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.890
Yeah, he's getting on my nerves.

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:39.480
<i>Sergeant Largo Potter and Corporal Brigitte Stark.</i>

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.680
<i>They're already expressing their hostility towards Welkin.</i>

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:44.210
<i>Well, not like I don't understand how they feel.</i>

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:47.030
First, there's one thing I'd like to tell you.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:51.560
What's the most important thing in combat?

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:52.990
Do you know?

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:57.210
Isn't that obvious? It's all about the experience!

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:03.630
Yes, I can't deny that experience is important, but it's not the most important thing.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.720
Your lives are what's most important.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:13.390
What nonsense.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:17.640
You'll probably go through a lot as the fighting continues.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:21.230
Painful times, fun times, happy times, and sad times.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:26.090
But you can't experience any of them if you're not alive.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:28.470
If you die, it's all over.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:33.160
No matter what kind of fix you get yourself in, as long as you're alive, there's still hope.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:36.120
I want you to remember that.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.020
Don't die!

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:44.630
As long as I'm leader of this squad, I swear that I will do my utmost best to protect your lives.

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:49.090
So I hope that you'll do your utmost best to stay alive, too.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:50.830
That is all.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:03.980
"No matter what kind of fix you get yourself in, as long as you're alive, there's still hope.", he said.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:06.950
Isn't that just great?

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:10.840
The things well-to-do kids from the university say sure are different.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.120
Indeed.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:15.600
He was trying to win us over with his lame speech.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.630
But we really got the short end of the stick.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:21.650
Of all people, we had to get that kind of person has our leader.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:27.800
But there's an even bigger problem here in this squad.

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:38.840
That girl in the cape?

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:42.150
Yeah, she's definitely a Darcsen.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:50.430
The situation holds that our line of defense has been pushed further into our territory by the Imperial Army's invasion.

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:53.200
But we have no intention of letting them pass.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:58.700
Currently, the Military, including the Militia, is in the process of reorganising its forces.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:03.960
Once we complete preparations, we will proceed to retaliate swiftly.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:06.590
Our first objective is Vasel Town.

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:07.820
Vasel...

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:11.010
As you already know, Vasel is a vital point of transportation.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:17.970
The Vasel Bridge, in particular, is a crucial location that connects the main road to the capital city of Randgriz.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:23.010
In other words, they already have us at knife point.

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:23.940
Exactly.

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:29.190
The tide will turn in favour of the side that gains control of the bridge.

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:34.820
After the Militia's reorganization is complete, we will sortie for Vasel Town immediately.

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:38.460
All squads, make preparations for move-out.

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:39.220
That's all.

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:40.790
Yes, Ma'am!

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:00.650
Alicia.

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:02.270
W-What?

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:07.330
If you're so uptight now, won't you lose your breath when the time comes?

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:11.440
Then do you want me to be happy-go-lucky like some squad leader?

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:14.070
You're pretty unforgiving.

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:16.190
But yeah, that's about right.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:19.120
Honestly... you...

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.430
You see, the Military already departed before we did,

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:26.820
so perhaps Vasel is already under our control.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:28.640
I see it! It's Vasel Town!

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:44.150
It seems the situation isn't going like we hoped.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:50.610
Battle is at a deadlock when we've only just arrived, huh?

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:55.570
The Military attempted to cross the bridge but were taken out, instead.

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:56.640
That can't be avoided.

00:09:57.370 --> 00:10:02.620
The other bridges have been destroyed, and there's no other place to cross the river.

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:06.400
If so, the battle here may drag on for quite a while.

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:11.360
Yes. If we make any reckless moves, we'll only increase the number of casualties.

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:13.690
I've had it with you.

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:15.950
Get out of our sight this instant.

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:17.750
Why?

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:21.530
What? You need me to tell it to your face?

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:23.420
Hey, what are you doing?

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:25.100
You're just in time.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:28.820
Mister Commander, let me make this clear.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:30.820
What do you mean?

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:32.540
Isn't it obvious?

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:34.920
I refuse to fight alongside a Darcsen.

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:36.280
Hey, you-

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.170
Same sentiments here.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:42.440
The Darcsens are, from ages ago, said to bring disaster.

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:43.620
Hey, everyone-

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.260
Don't even try.

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:50.570
Nobody will follow the orders of a boy who has never seen real battle before.

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:53.040
She's an eyesore.

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:56.640
Girl's got the nerve to prance around in her Darcsen cloth.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:59.280
It's true that I'm a Darcsen.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:02.540
But like you all, I'm also human.

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:07.360
Besides, the Darcsen Calamity is just a myth with no scientific evidence to back it up.

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:11.450
What did you say? Do you mean I'm making a false accusation?

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:13.630
All right! Let's make a bet then!

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:18.510
You don't want to follow my orders.

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:21.010
I want you to follow my orders.

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:23.480
Then the quickest solution is to make a bet.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:27.340
You're kidding! Are you saying you want to toss a coin at a time like this?

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:33.120
The main question is whether or not I'm qualified to be a commander, isn't it?

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:35.060
Then give me two days.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:36.860
In two days, we'll have the verdict.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:38.490
Welkin?

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:39.850
I promise you.

00:11:39.850 --> 00:11:46.560
Within forty-eight hours, I shall recapture that bridge with just Squad 7.

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:49.020
You're not out of your mind, are you?

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:53.480
If I fail, I shall resign as squad leader.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:56.550
If I succeed, everyone must follow my orders.

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:57.230
Are you all fine with that?

00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:00.790
You won't go back on your word, right?

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:02.030
Don't regret what you said.

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:05.410
We've got a deal then.

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:10.080
Seriously, what were you thinking?

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:13.660
Even if you ask me...

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:18.920
Oh, it's a travelling swallow.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:22.920
If the Military couldn't do it, how will we be able to?

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:28.330
Besides, recapturing the bridge within two days is surely impossible.

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:32.450
Are you worried about me?

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:34.920
O-Of course not!

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:37.900
Well, we'll cross that bridge when we come to it.{GROAN}

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:41.070
What did you do to become that optimistic?

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:47.550
Speaking of optimism, I believe tomorrow morning's weather is going to be great.

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:49.060
For me, that is.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:53.010
I said two days, but it's going to be faster than I thought.

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:56.640
Alicia, relay this to the others.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:13:00.000
Commence operation tomorrow morning at 0500.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.770
<i>It's hopeless. I don't understand at all.</i>

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:05.430
<i>What the heck is this man thinking?</i>

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:12.830
Hey, Wel... Sir.

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:14.880
It's all right, just call me Welkin.

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:18.110
Then Welkin, did you know there was going to be fog?

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:25.830
Fog is something that rises when air with water vapour is cooled.

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:29.660
Besides, the travelling swallows were flying.

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:30.910
Swallows?

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:37.150
When the travelling swallow flies low, it's
proof that air in the higher altitudes is cold.

00:13:37.150 --> 00:13:39.710
Then... that bird yesterday...

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:42.500
Well, that's how it is.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:45.660
Now then, things are going to get busy around here.

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:52.200
We, Squad 7, are going launch a surprise attack on the enemy's point of defense on the eastern bank.

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:53.590
What the hell are you saying?

00:13:53.590 --> 00:13:57.080
Even if there's fog, there's no way we can make it across the bridge with this number of people!

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.140
We're not going to use the bridge.

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:02.740
We'll just cross the river.

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:04.890
You want us to charge without a tank?

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:06.280
It's like you're telling us to die-

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:09.100
Don't worry. We'll use the tank too.

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:11.890
Are you going to fly it through the sky?

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:13.220
Something like that.

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:16.010
But I won't be crossing the sky. I'll be crossing the water.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:21.070
We're going to cross the river in this Edelweiss.

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:27.280
Are you taking us for fools? A tank is something that moves on land, not in water!

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:29.570
I don't think you're sane.

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:32.970
I've never heard of a tank crossing a river.

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:34.420
That's why...

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:37.910
That's why we're going to do it.

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:41.800
Here are the details of the battle plan.

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:46.300
The Edelweiss will head for the east bank immediately.

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:48.890
In the meantime, the foot soldiers will await further orders on the battlefield.

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:55.100
After you see signs of allied fire, go all out to take control of the enemy base.

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:56.530
Right, everyone.

00:14:56.530 --> 00:14:59.200
This is the first mission of Squad 7.

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:00.850
Let's go for it!

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:06.300
Is he serious about doing this?

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:09.620
Welkin.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:11.890
I'm sorry.

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.220
It's all because of me...

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:16.130
It's all right. On the contrary, you helped me a lot.

00:15:16.130 --> 00:15:20.830
It's something I can't avoid if I want to gain command of the squad.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:25.570
Besides, this plan would never have happened without you.

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:31.060
Though, I won't know how effective the waterproof modifications are without putting them to the test.

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:34.530
Sorry for making you accompany me on this reckless plan.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:40.830
No, it's fine. I have faith in both you and the Edelweiss.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:44.410
Are we ready to go?

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:45.750
Yes.

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:46.650
Good.

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:47.800
Commence operation!

00:15:53.710 --> 00:15:56.320
Come, let's begin, too.

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:07.070
Another 300 meters before we reach the opposite shore.

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:10.030
Another 2 minutes, 40 seconds before the estimated diving time limit is exceeded.

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:12.240
I'm counting on you, Edelweiss.

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:15.170
Another 250 meters to the shore.

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:30.130
<i>Welkin.</i>

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:34.510
Another 200 meters.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:36.250
Rev it up!

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:38.840
If the engine stalls on us, the mission is a failure.

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:40.260
Understood.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:59.810
What's happening?

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:02.120
It's already been three minutes.

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:07.530
What's wrong?

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.640
No, it's nothing.

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:28.990
River crossing successful!

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:29.690
Purging modifications.

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:33.520
All right! Let's commence our attack!

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:47.990
That bastard really made it across...

00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:49.350
Move! {he says something like "begin moving" (idou kaishi), god I hate gundamspeak}

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:51.070
Don't slow down!

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:53.820
Don't let them find out the true size of our force!

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:54.700
Understood!

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:04.830
Enemy attack!

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:05.670
How many of them?!

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:07.180
We don't know!

00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:08.580
Impossible. Where the hell did they-

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:27.080
20 degrees to the right! Fire! {What's he saying this for, he's the one in control of the turret}

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:40.780
Don't hold back! Concentrate your firepower to the north!

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:49.790
We're completely surrounded! It's... hopeless.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.600
Good work, everyone.

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:24.520
Looks like everything went just as planned.{Just as Keikaku, TL Note: Keikaku means plan.}

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:30.270
You're a pretty amazing guy.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:34.830
It's a promise! Now, you all must follow the orders of the commander.

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:35.730
Understood?

00:19:36.140 --> 00:19:40.060
Well, I'm fine with listening to the commander.

00:19:40.550 --> 00:19:45.170
But there's no way I'd agree to a Darcsen.

00:19:45.170 --> 00:19:47.120
Hey, what do you mean by that?

00:19:51.650 --> 00:19:52.430
Wait!

00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:55.170
Alicia, it's all right. I'm used to it already.

00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:56.940
Isara...

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:14.700
See? I told you Welkin's a weirdo.

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:16.820
I hang out with him because I like that side of him.

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:19.000
I don't know what he thinks about me, though.

00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:22.280
Oh, right... I'm Faldio Landzaat.

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:23.820
I've known him since university.

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:27.710
I'm his buddy, guardian, and a busybody in general.

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:31.430
Next time on Valkyria Chronicles, Chapter 4.

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:32.910
A  Brief Holiday.

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:39.700
In the aeons of history weaved by man, will you look for its source together with me?

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:39.930
Chapter 4:

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:39.930
Brief Holiday
